A||||15||REDHOTT88||Succesful Torsion rod removal from decklid.. gain of 6HP!!!||||12||
Z||000000||REDHOTT88||12-10-2001||04:31 PM||||Thank you guys for the info on torsion rod removal from the deklid hinges.. you know who you are!   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smiley_watchout.gif"><P>I was able to take out my broken hinge and torsion rods (without breaking rear window!) and now am ready for Rodney D's strut kit.<P>I actually took a hacksaw and cut them at the top, then removed decklid. (I didn't have the proper torx screwdriver. But was able to borrow one after the fact to remove the screws from hinge.) The rods were tough to deal with but I got them out without much grief.<P>I took my broken hinge to a mechanic , he torched out the snapped pin and replaced it with a metal rod saving me the hassle of finding a new hinge. I just repainted the hinges and put em back in!<P>I think the torsion rods weigh about 3.2 lbs. and I am now experiencing a gain of 6HP due to their removal!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Steve<BR><B>1988 Formula 2.8L</B> V6 5 speed <BR><FONT COLOR="ffoooo"> (Red and shiny all over!)</FONT><p>[This message has been edited by REDHOTT88 (edited 12-10-2001).]||||reg||12
Z||000001||Kasdan||12-10-2001||04:48 PM||||Are you serious?  I doubt that little weight would get you 6hp, lol<P>------------------<BR>Tyler Morgan, 1986 GT<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/kassig2.gif">                  <BR>Aftermarket Power Steering, Rebuilt 2.8<BR>http://www.geocities.com/mtyler14/index.html||||reg||1
Z||000002||Butter||12-10-2001||05:01 PM||||If you change the muffler bearings you can gain another 6hp!<P>------------------<BR> <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/buttersig_1.gif"> ||||reg||7
Z||000003||REDHOTT88||12-10-2001||05:07 PM||||Actually it was only 5.7 on the dyno. but I rounded up!!! Ha Ha  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>(Hey thats what the ricers told me anyway!!!)<P>||||reg||1
Z||000004||REDHOTT88||12-10-2001||05:40 PM||||I also noticed that my rear suspension is much higher. I might have to get a lowering kit!!!  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif">||||reg||1
